# gameboy.skin — 4-shade olive-green DMG LCD, everything reads as one dot-matrix screen
name gameboy

# LCD dot texture: light dither on dark, the classic Game Boy screen grain
texture ░

# desktop: lightest shade dither over darkest shade — max LCD contrast
desk 15 0

# paper: darkest bg, mid-light ink — readable body text on the "screen"
paper 0 11

# dialog: darkest bg (via slot 8, also mapped darkest), lightest ink for accent panes
dialog 8 15

# chrome must be explicit — this is a dark skin
framePassive 130
frameActive 11
# menu: mid-light bar, black-ish ink for the strongest bar/text split available
menu 112

dim 8
accent 11
floor 15 0

ok 10
warn 14

# All 16 CGA slots collapse onto the four authentic DMG greens by brightness
# band — this is the whole point of the skin: there is no colour, only shade.
# darkest #0F380F  dark #306230  light #8BAC0F  lightest #9BBC0F
pal0 #0F380F
pal1 #306230
pal2 #306230
pal3 #8BAC0F
pal4 #306230
pal5 #306230
pal6 #306230
pal7 #8BAC0F
pal8 #0F380F
pal9 #8BAC0F
pal10 #8BAC0F
pal11 #9BBC0F
pal12 #8BAC0F
pal13 #8BAC0F
pal14 #9BBC0F
pal15 #9BBC0F
